  "chapters": [
    {
      "title": "Same elements. New possibilities.",
      "category": "UX / Continuity",
      "text": "Watch this. A profile becomes an editor. A thumbnail becomes the hero. These are the same live elements, keeping their identity as the interface changes around them.",
      "at": 0.0
    },
    {
      "title": "A whole interface, choreographed.",
      "category": "UX / Orchestration",
      "text": "Now coordinate the whole scene. Messages make room for each other. Change direction mid-flight, and the motion responds. Open a card, and everything else knows where to go.",
      "at": 9.567
    },
    {
      "title": "Time becomes a control.",
      "category": "Interaction / Time",
      "text": "Even time becomes interactive. Scrub the kiln backwards: the app reconstructs what happened. Then flick a puck, and watch the choreography follow the consequences of your gesture.",
      "at": 18.75
    },
    {
      "title": "The interface enters space.",
      "category": "Spatial computing",
      "text": "Now give the interface depth. Open a real app inside a spatial device. Fly into a photograph. The camera and the interface share the same choreography, so space becomes part of the interaction.",
      "at": 28.004
    },
    {
      "title": "Direct it. Scrub it. Build it.",
      "category": "Filmmaking / Build Order",
      "text": "And now, direct a film. One continuous camera move carries the story. Scrub an entire edit, then finish in Build Order: arrange the beats, retime the reveal, and play it again. That is Choreo.",
      "at": 38.58
    }
  ],
